  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Replaced rank plus transpose-HNF-transform with FLINT nullspace, exact lattice saturation, and final row HNF. The canonical basis matches SageMath on 87 structured/random/skew cases, including large integers and degenerate shapes; the existing 300-round ASan/UBSan/leak lifecycle harness passes. On the deterministic 100x150 workload the candidate measured 696 ms versus 1337 ms for the previous generated implementation and 895 ms for SageMath.",
    "risks": [
      "The saturation proof depends on FLINT HNF orientation: the leading nullity rows of HNF(B^T), transposed, are a nonsingular column-basis matrix for the lattice generated by B. Exact divisibility is checked before division and failure is reported instead of weakening the result.",
      "The focused portable tier was not used as a final receipt because this lane branched before two newly-added tests were assigned to the runner manifest and a concurrent incomplete build removed generated runtime-cache files; architecture, strict Python, focused oracle, lifecycle sanitizer, and benchmark validation pass."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Integration lane should rebuild the FLINT generated adapter from the merged header and rerun the focused tests plus the current portable tier."
    ]
  }
